    <string name="loc_title">Know when you are home</string>
    <string name="loc_text">To tell the house you are on your home Wi-Fi, Android lets the app read the network\'s name only with the location permission. The app never reads or sends where you are, only whether this network is the house\'s.</string>
    <string name="loc_ok">Continue</string>
    <string name="loc_later">Not now</string>
    <string name="bgloc_title">Read the Wi-Fi name in the background</string>
    <string name="bgloc_text">The house reads your Wi-Fi name whenever the phone talks to it, also when the app is closed. Android allows that only with the location access \"Allow all the time\". The location itself is never read or sent. You can decline: the house then tells home from away by the network address alone.</string>
